<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia's SFE wheat futures tend higher.</title>
<headline>Australia's SFE wheat futures tend higher.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Traded Sydney Futures Exchange (SFE) wheat contracts tended higher on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The July 1997 contract rose A$2 to A$196 a tonne on a volume of only one trade while the November 1997 contract gained A$1 to A$168 on a volume of five lots.</p>
<p>But the most active January 1998 contract was unchanged on Monday's settlement at A$166 a tonne on a volume of 13 lots.</p>
<p>Nearby settlement prices tended lower and distant prices higher.</p>
